From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] ipv6: don't restart a finished dump of a single table

A route dump restricted to one table ("ip -6 route show table main", and
"ip -6 route show dev X", which implies the main table) never ended: once
fib6_dump_table() had walked the whole table, inet6_dump_fib() returned
the skb length, netlink called it again, and with the walker idle the next
fib6_dump_table() started a new walk from the root. The same routes came
back forever and iproute2 spun a CPU core (pmOS's routewrangler runs
exactly this dump). Remember in cb->args[0] that the table is done, as
upstream's inet6_dump_fib() does.
---
--- a/net/ipv6/ip6_fib.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/ip6_fib.c
@@ -635,7 +635,11 @@
 			return -ENOENT;
 		}

-		res = fib6_dump_table(tb, skb, cb);
+		if (!cb->args[0]) {
+			res = fib6_dump_table(tb, skb, cb);
+			if (!res)
+				cb->args[0] = 1;
+		}
 		goto out;
 	}

